sections.body:
At B2, a summary must keep the **reasoning** of the text, not just its topic: who says what, what they argue, and how the ideas connect. Method:

1. read the text twice; find the **central question** and the **author's position**;
2. identify the **main arguments** (often one per paragraph) and how they are linked (cause, opposition, concession…);
3. reformulate in your own words — no copying sentences — and keep the logical connectors;
4. stay neutral: no personal opinion in the summary itself;
5. respect the length (about a quarter or a third of the original).
